  clock: 3  # 6738
  nonce: '6738'  # 6738
  message: "Fixed in PR #1771. Checked all 61 unwired find_*_files helpers (59 test-only, plus fortran and verilog, whose helper fed only the profile count). Only D's and Hack's filtered differently from the analyzer; clojure's helper also differed in the other direction (it returned .edn files the analyzer skips). D: DAnalyzer._find_source_files -> find_d_files, also registered as D's find_files for the profile. Hack: HackAnalyzer._find_source_files -> find_hack_files; the <?hh sniff moved to discovery.classify_dot_php_file, which find_php_files also applies, so PHP skips Hack files. The other 59 delegate to _analyzer._find_source_files. Guard: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_discovery_helper_wiring.py fails on any helper that is neither called by production code nor delegating. Behavioral evidence (live repro on dev after merge): dir with main.d='main.o: main.c foo.h' + app.d='module app; void run() {}' -> analyze_d run.files_analyzed == 1 (was 2), symbols only from app.d, _detect_languages()['d'].files == 1. Production-path tests: test_d.py::TestDiscoveryIsTheHelper, test_php.py::TestFindPhpFiles::test_skips_hack_files. Smart-test: 22,233 passed, 5 failed; the 5 were fixed (3 line citations re-anchored, the clojure .edn test updated, my PHP test's path assertion), and those 5 files re-run with plain pytest: 191 passed. CI passed before merge."  # 6738
